{"name":"Civara","hex":"#c56138","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Kasaya (clothing)","blocks":[{"text":"Kāṣāya are the robes of fully ordained Buddhist monks and nuns, named after a brown or saffron dye. In Sanskrit and Pali, these robes are also given the more general term cīvara, which references the robes without regard to color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Buddhist_monk_dresses_in_yellow_rope.jpg/330px-Buddhist_monk_dresses_in_yellow_rope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kasaya_(clothing)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Gandhara_Buddha_%28tnm%29.jpeg/500px-Gandhara_Buddha_%28tnm%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Gandhara_Buddha_%28tnm%29.jpeg/1280px-Gandhara_Buddha_%28tnm%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Gandhara_Buddha_%28tnm%29.jpeg/500px-Gandhara_Buddha_%28tnm%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An early representation of the Buddha wearing kāṣāya robes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGandhara_Buddha_(tnm).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Astasahasrika_Prajnaparamita_Victory_Over_Mara.jpeg/330px-Astasahasrika_Prajnaparamita_Victory_Over_Mara.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Astasahasrika_Prajnaparamita_Victory_Over_Mara.jpeg/330px-Astasahasrika_Prajnaparamita_Victory_Over_Mara.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indian depiction of the Buddha wearing red robes. Sanskrit manuscript. Nāl